#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059375 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "14e05d4f-373c-5d1f-aa59-7ee52466480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-14762" :question/problem "Find the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/assets/8e7935fce161e2a1ed706ec03bb5cd202e8c4650ba01ca5e4633f9f1c121d04a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059376 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/id #uuid "d7516cec-bd96-59db-98cd-5d82e41fa719" :question/math-academy-id "e-14763" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075636/assets/21cd71e00c682ad1117b9ae126adcbeb8e4c55769c73eae1e1169534f2a01d4a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059377 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/id #uuid "7780340c-43d6-5d38-9270-865914098218" :question/math-academy-id "e-14764" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a191dba-16dd-5b91-b92c-74456c9286df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303309} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b00579-93ef-5741-b329-98cc98e20e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303310} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e1a3d4-3256-56a2-8579-d0cb7725057f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303311} {:answer/id #uuid "d91db950-9a7f-5572-9414-c66c3ae0f4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303312} {:answer/id #uuid "8dac9c91-67ef-5130-939b-a0b625916607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a191dba-16dd-5b91-b92c-74456c9286df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303309} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5536c7-7d93-5b6f-bcb0-08074eb5662e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1de7b7b6-d74a-53dc-9249-a5265a42e232" :question/math-academy-id "q-128476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\n- $T$ is a singular matrix\n- $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $det(T)=-30$\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba948d9a-0adb-5139-b992-7e3ef6211177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382679} {:answer/id #uuid "c4dbae3e-5235-57a9-9aa9-f81a548c19fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382680} {:answer/id #uuid "328ff454-e0e9-585e-a85a-9fa542f2a95d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382681} {:answer/id #uuid "f00d4c1f-15cf-5b01-be55-a79c1f05202c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382682} {:answer/id #uuid "678d2bd2-d11f-5579-b305-c9942bcd3381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "678d2bd2-d11f-5579-b305-c9942bcd3381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382683} :answer-field/id #uuid "04e27527-4ac1-5c1c-91d9-a7ed3ee291c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a11fa43-6c7e-5600-9b6b-53466b56fa48" :question/math-academy-id "q-128500" :question/problem "Given that\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(B)=12,$ find the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ y & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ y & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot (1-y)-5\\cdot (2-2y) \\\\  & =12y-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $12,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-12 & =12 \\\\ 12y & =24 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186320311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5864ebc-bd7f-518a-ae9b-cfcd1031f011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320313} {:answer/id #uuid "e053aafa-15e9-53d8-b693-05a611f29ea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320314} {:answer/id #uuid "8d870840-8390-59b1-9bf4-6f4cc2c09cf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320315} {:answer/id #uuid "308cd1c5-fdc4-50d9-a9ee-e91c144ed145" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320316} {:answer/id #uuid "d6454265-e507-5721-bd63-f7e365b93e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e053aafa-15e9-53d8-b693-05a611f29ea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320314} :answer-field/id #uuid "653b22c2-ac63-55f3-b4fb-7b1a85208b53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320312}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30a80f14-b653-5ec9-a12d-20d43bb40f91" :question/math-academy-id "q-128506" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-29$, find all the possible values of $m.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-6|\\begin{aligned}m & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+m|\\begin{aligned}m & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-0)-6(m-0)+m(m-6) \\\\  & =3-6m+{m}^{2}-6m \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-12m+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-29,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-12m+3 & =-29 \\\\ {m}^{2}-12m+32 & =0 \\\\ m & =\\frac{-(-12)\\pm \\sqrt{{12}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 32}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=4$ and $m=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53d6979c-b8d7-57d1-9f38-f4a05a09e7d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ and $-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382686} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b8eb22-16db-5bab-8316-457b57a2c976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382687} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a82094-bf6c-5d9c-afc6-58825a1ac5dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382688} {:answer/id #uuid "ed49e64d-0484-58a6-8db9-8f727d6e97d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382689} {:answer/id #uuid "fa20b06c-807e-5188-a281-2600af857b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1a82094-bf6c-5d9c-afc6-58825a1ac5dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382688} :answer-field/id #uuid "726c649d-a64b-570b-a9ab-126c08e00ae0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dbd44e55-ce0f-5b5b-8e89-0724c2b1c4da" :question/math-academy-id "q-130580" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $22$, find all the possible values of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}5 & x \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(x-14)-2x(5-21)+3(10-3x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-14x+32x+30-9x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+9x+30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $22,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+9x+30 & =22 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9x+8 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{{9}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 8}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-8,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-8$ and $x=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20471aec-848e-513e-968a-d6aec97caa96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303323} {:answer/id #uuid "b476adf8-40ae-54da-ac98-df291a8dd1ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303324} {:answer/id #uuid "09c5767d-a3b0-5d1a-860a-026fafd6510c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303325} {:answer/id #uuid "f5001a26-00b9-5b68-b868-a2749147bd0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303326} {:answer/id #uuid "e19af8f1-f3a5-5db5-ac86-072cb48385c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e19af8f1-f3a5-5db5-ac86-072cb48385c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303327} :answer-field/id #uuid "59e39d2d-4575-5e43-a400-caa5668def86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01aa8d57-113b-5436-b1ef-e962e4723b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-18256" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}]$\n is $81,$ find all the possible values of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ y & -5\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}-3y & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-3y & -2 \\\\ 2 & y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (10-y)-2\\cdot (15y-2)+3\\cdot (-3{y}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =40-4y-30y+4-9{y}^{2}+12 \\\\  & =-9{y}^{2}-34y+56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $81,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{y}^{2}-34y+56 & =81 \\\\ -9{y}^{2}-34y-25 & =0 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+34y+25 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{{34}^{2}-4\\cdot 9\\cdot 25}}{2\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{256}}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm 16}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-17\\pm 8}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $y=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff34e01-249d-5f34-a6ee-d7b6e18a50c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303341} {:answer/id #uuid "d14d2afd-862f-529e-bfcf-55965bdfb7a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d14d2afd-862f-529e-bfcf-55965bdfb7a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303342} :answer-field/id #uuid "18824b8b-d559-5060-91df-b38c33b99b4d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "711f7b0f-8038-59ce-9d0e-6b423dd7512d" :question/math-academy-id "q-280390" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],$ then $det(A)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2(0-0)-3(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbfce83b-d77a-539f-a673-3c1b57d43754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbfce83b-d77a-539f-a673-3c1b57d43754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382693} :answer-field/id #uuid "b33d7a95-31e3-59e7-baff-78a70fb87d69" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4fcc1b0-90f4-51c2-8119-f777b876fe0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4fcc1b0-90f4-51c2-8119-f777b876fe0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382695} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed8b1ec8-ea6a-55e7-a205-8e82e5998c39" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "91bf5b01-bba4-5542-be99-561e28debf43" :question/math-academy-id "q-280540" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of $[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is $32$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}x & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+0 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(-2\\cdot 0-(-1)(4))-3(x\\cdot 0-(-1)(1)) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(4)-3(1) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-8-3 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $32$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-11 & =32 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =43 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{43}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{43}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "979859e4-b60c-548d-8da6-b180400e1b07" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a865554-0a16-5080-a9ac-454763f1b02a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303345} {:answer/id #uuid "70a3288c-9a8b-5258-a31a-e86f7929ead4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303346} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf721f7-87c3-51fa-aaf3-91839fc65583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303347} {:answer/id #uuid "31b4cba5-feaf-5b8a-a451-d244cad17919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303348} {:answer/id #uuid "5edc7390-a20c-5673-9b84-c60171d426fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cf721f7-87c3-51fa-aaf3-91839fc65583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303347} :answer-field/id #uuid "216ec6d2-dd2c-5323-